IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Common Informers (Parliamentary Disqualifications) Act 1975 (Cth) — THE
-- NOUNS, RULES AND TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00250.txt (compilation C2008C00320).
-- Seat: the senator or member sued.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Suit` HAS
    -- s 3(1): a person "declared by the Constitution to be incapable of so
    -- sitting" — a finding
    `I was incapable of sitting`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `days I am proved to have sat`                      IS A LIST OF DATE
    `suit instituted on`                                IS A DATE
    `process served on`                                 IS A DATE
    -- s 3(3)
    `days already penalised`                            IS A LIST OF DATE

DECLARE `Common informer position` HAS
    `the sum I can be made to pay`                      IS A NUMBER
    `I can be sued under s 46 of the Constitution`      IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 3(2): "A suit under this section shall not relate to any sitting ... at a
-- time earlier than 12 months before the day on which the suit is
-- instituted."
@ref s 3(2)
GIVEN s IS A `Suit`
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest sitting day that counts for` s MEANS
    `add months` (s's `suit instituted on`) (0 MINUS 12)

-- Each day once: "$200 for every day" (s 3(1)(b)), and no day penalised
-- twice (s 3(3)) (changed after the independent pass).
GIVEN ds IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`each day once` ds MEANS
    CONSIDER ds
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF elem d rest
        THEN `each day once` rest
        ELSE d FOLLOWED BY (`each day once` rest)

-- The days that count: within s 3(2), and not already penalised (s 3(3)).
@ref s 3(2)-(3)
GIVEN s IS A `Suit`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the days that count for` s MEANS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD d AT LEAST `the earliest sitting day that counts for` s AND NOT (elem d (s's `days already penalised`)))
           (`each day once` (s's `days I am proved to have sat`))

-- s 3(1): "(a) $200 in respect of his or her having so sat on or before the
-- day on which the originating process in the suit is served ...; and (b)
-- $200 for every day, subsequent to that day, on which he or she is proved in
-- the suit to have so sat."
@ref s 3
@export The sum I can be made to pay a common informer for sitting in Parliament while incapable, under s 3 of the Common Informers (Parliamentary Disqualifications) Act 1975 (Cth): $200 if I so sat on or before the day the originating process was served, plus $200 for each later day I am proved to have so sat; counting no sitting earlier than 12 months before the suit was instituted, and no day already penalised. Nil if I was not incapable. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Suit`  @desc The finding of incapacity, the sitting days, the dates of institution and service, and days already penalised
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum I can be made to pay for` s MEANS
    IF NOT (s's `I was incapable of sitting`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE beforeService PLUS 200 TIMES (sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD 1) after))
    WHERE
        days MEANS `the days that count for` s
        after MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD d GREATER THAN s's `process served on`) days
        beforeService MEANS
            IF any (GIVEN d YIELD d AT MOST s's `process served on`) days
            THEN 200
            ELSE 0

§ `The top-level goal`

-- s 4: "a person is not liable to pay any sum under section 46 of the
-- Constitution and no suit shall be instituted ... in pursuance of that
-- section."
@ref ss 3-4
@export default The position of a senator or member sued for sitting while incapable, under the Common Informers (Parliamentary Disqualifications) Act 1975 (Cth): the sum they can be made to pay (s 3), and that no suit lies under s 46 of the Constitution (s 4). Such suits are heard only in the High Court (s 5). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Suit`  @desc The suit
GIVETH A `Common informer position`
`the common informer position for` s MEANS
    `Common informer position` WITH
        `the sum I can be made to pay`                  IS `the sum I can be made to pay for` s
        `I can be sued under s 46 of the Constitution`  IS FALSE
